1. Scope

This license covers the Flux Pylons source code, compiled mod, project-created
assets and documentation supplied with this license (the "Project"). Materials
identified as third-party work remain under their own licenses. In particular,
the NeoForged MDK notice in TEMPLATE_LICENSE.txt is unchanged.

2. Playing, research and private changes

You may download, install, run and make necessary local or backup copies of the
Project. You may run the official mod on a Minecraft client or server. You may
inspect source code you lawfully obtain and make private changes for learning,
research, testing and preparing contributions to the official project.

These permissions do not authorize distributing a modified build, operating a
modified version as a separate public mod project, or incorporating Project code
or assets into another distributed product.

3. Contributions

You may submit patches, improvements and other contributions to the official
Flux Pylons project. You may maintain a source-only fork for preparing and
reviewing such contributions, clearly identified as a contribution fork. This
exception does not authorize publishing fork binaries or maintaining a separate
release, port, successor or feature variant.

You retain ownership of your original contributions. By intentionally submitting
a contribution for inclusion, you grant the maintainers permission to use,
modify and distribute it as part of the official Project under this license.
You must have the authority to grant those permissions.

4. Redistribution and modpacks

You may redistribute unmodified official releases of the compiled mod, including
through third-party launchers, download mirrors, modpacks and server packs,
without asking for permission. Keep the mod JAR unchanged, retain its copyright
and license notices, credit Flux Pylons and ZeroTheAbsolute, and link to an
official project page. Include this license with the download or pack when it
is not already included in the JAR. Ordinary modpack configuration, scripts and
resource-pack overrides do not modify the JAR and are permitted; this does not
permit copying Project code or assets into those overrides.

These redistribution permissions also apply to official Flux Pylons releases
previously supplied under Flux Pylons License 1.0. You do not need to edit those
JARs to replace their embedded license; supply this license alongside them.

Except for the permissions in this license or separate written permission from
ZeroTheAbsolute, you may not distribute modified builds, renamed copies, ports,
forks as separate mods, versions with added features, or Project source code or
assets for reuse in another distributed mod or product. Modpack inclusion does
not grant permission to distribute a derivative version of Flux Pylons.

5. Screenshots, videos and research reports

You may publish gameplay screenshots, videos, reviews and research findings,
including monetized videos, with reasonable attribution. This permission does
not authorize distributing Project source, assets or binaries beyond the other
permissions in this license. Rights you independently have under applicable
law, including fair use and other copyright exceptions, are unaffected.

6. Names and notices

Keep applicable copyright and license notices with every permitted copy. Do not
present your work as an official Flux Pylons release or imply endorsement by
ZeroTheAbsolute. Descriptive references and attribution are permitted; no
